      "defect": "A bucket tagged with a sensitive-data classification (PHI, PII, or confidential) is exposed via public read or public list. The tag declares the data's sensitivity; the access state contradicts that declaration.\n",
      "infection": "Any internet caller can fetch the sensitive objects via anonymous GET or enumerate them via anonymous ListBucket. Search engines and compliance scanners specifically match data-classification tags against access state, so a single tagged-sensitive + public bucket becomes the highest-priority finding in most posture dashboards. Regulators treat the classification tag as evidence of awareness: the organization has labeled this data sensitive and nonetheless exposed it publicly, which weakens claims of accidental oversight.\n",
      "failure": "Regulated-data breach. PHI exposure triggers HIPAA breach notification; PII exposure triggers GDPR/CCPA obligations; confidential data exposure typically triggers contractual disclosure and customer notification. Remediation scope is bounded by the exposure window — audit CloudTrail to bound who accessed during that window and produce the notification roster.\n",
      "delta": [
